{100}{Portrait
This is you.}
{101}{Character Info
This is some basic personal information.}
{102}{Alignment Meter
This is your alignment, a measure of how good or evil you are.}
{103}{Available Points
These are the points available to spend on improving yourself. You get one point each time you go up a level.}
{104}{Level
This is your current level. The experience points you gain in the game will increase your level and provide more points to spend on improving yourself.}
{105}{Experience Needed
This is the number of experience points you need to go up to the next level.}
{106}{Health
Damage will reduce your hit points, and when it reaches 0, you die. Health is based on Strength and Willpower.}
{107}{Fatigue
Casting, encumbrance, and some damage will reduce your fatigue points, and when it reaches 0, you pass out. Fatigue is based on Constitution and Willpower.}
{108}{Magick Tech Meter
This scale displays your magickal-technological aptitude. The higher the needle, the more magickal you are. The lower, the more technological.}
{109}{Strength
Your physical muscle power, Strength determines how much damage you can inflict and absorb. Weapons have a minimum strength to operate them effectively.}
{110}{Constitution
The endurance limit of your body, Constitution determines your fatigue and resistance to poison and some spells.}
{111}{Dexterity
Your overall body coordination, Dexterity affects your default ability in more skills than any other stat.}
{112}{Beauty
Your physical appearance, Beauty affects the initial reaction of people to you.}
{113}{Intelligence
Your mental power, Intelligence affects several skills as well as being the limiting factor in your learning of spells and technological skills.}
{114}{Willpower
The ability to resist mental influences, Willpower affects your ability to haggle and also contributes to your hit points, fatigue and certain spell resistances.}
{115}{Perception
The ability for you to notice your surroundings, Perception also affects your ability to use ranged weapons effectively.}
{116}{Charisma
The sum of your personality and charm, Charisma affects your ability to persuade others and change their initial reaction to you.}
{117}{Derived Stats
These are stats that are based on your basic stats above. Spells and items may modify these as well.}
{118}{Carry Weight
This is the total amount of equipment you can carry and is based on Strength.}
{119}{Damage Bonus
This is extra damage inflicted by any melee attack and is based on Strength.}
{120}{Armor Class Adjustment
This is an improvement to your AC which makes you harder to hit. This is based on Dexterity.}
{121}{Speed
The higher your Speed, the faster you move and the more attacks you make. Speed can be modified by encumbrance and weapon choice. Speed is based on Dexterity.}
{122}{Heal Rate
This is the rate at which you recover your hit points and is based on Constitution.}
{123}{Poison Recovery
This is the rate at which you metabolize poison and reduce the damage taken by it. It is based on Constitution.}
{124}{Reaction Modifier
This is the adjustment to the initial reaction that others have to you. It is based on Beauty.}
{125}{Maximum Followers
This is the maximum number of people who follow you because of your leadership. It is based on Charisma.}
{126}{Resistance
You begin with five basic resistances that can range from 0 to 95%. Items, background, race, and magick can modify all resistances.}
{127}{Damage Resistance
This is a general resistance to damage caused by weapons and physical attacks.}
{128}{Magick Resistance
This is resistance to magick spells and effects. Unlike Technological Aptitude, magick resistance does not affect your use of items or spells.}
{129}{Fire Resistance
This is resistance to damage by fire and spells that produce fire.}
{130}{Poison Resistance
This is resistance to damage caused by any kind of poisoning, whether natural, man-made, or supernatural. It is affected by Constitution.}
{131}{Electrical Resistance
This is resistance to damage by electricity and lightning from spells or technological devices.}
{132}{Skills
This button will activate the display of skills below. Skills come in four groups: Combat, Thieving, Social, and Technological.}
{133}{Technological Disciplines
This button will activate the display of technological disciplines below. There are eight disciplines, each with 7 available degrees.}
{134}{Spell Colleges
This button will activate the display of spell colleges below. There are 16 colleges, each with 5 available spells.}
{135}{Combat Skills
These are the skills used primarily to attack and defend oneself during combat.}
{136}{Thieving Skills
These are skills used primarily by thieves, although they have other noncriminal uses too.}
{137}{Social Skills
These are the skills you use on other people or in social situations.}
{138}{Technological Skills
These are skills that dabble in technology. Buying these skills will increase your Technological Aptitude.}
{139}{Current Degree
This is your current degree in the selected technological discipline. The number to the right is your expertise and controls what kinds of schematics you may use.}
{140}{Auto-Level Schemes
This button will activate the display of available auto-level schemes. These schemes spend your character points automatically.}
